# Cursor Rules — Placeholder Standard

## Rule: Placeholder Standard

Always use the Placeholder Standard ($PLC) for any placeholder values in code.

### Patterns

When generating code, replace any placeholder with `$PLC`:

- ✅ `const apiKey = "$PLC_API";`
- ✅ `export const TOKEN = "$PLC";`
- ✅ `config: { token: "$PLC" }`
- ❌ `const apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY";` (deprecated)
- ❌ `const token = "example";` (deprecated)

### Auto-complete

When a user types "placeholder" or "test token", suggest:

```typescript
$PLC  // default placeholder
$PLC_API  // for API keys
$PLC_CONFIG  // for configs
